I look at my family.
"I am not alone here," I say.
"I have a friend."
My mother looks surprised.
"A friend?" she asks.
"Yes," I say.
"Her name is Nina."
"She is my neighbour."
"And she is from Denmark."
"A Danish friend!"
"That is lovely, sweetheart," she says.
My father nods.
"That is good, Maya," he says.
